NOTE 449: the a5dc WIN-LOGIC is DEAD CODE due to a 2da2 signedness bug (board:0012).

DISCOVERY (gdb hardware watchpoint on g_mem+0x22da2): a5dc's guard `if (DAT_2000_2da2 != -1)` is ALWAYS
TRUE, so a5dc decrements 2da2 and early-returns every frame, NEVER running the side-count / win-check.
Cause: undefined2 = uint16_t (unsigned); `(uint16_t)0xffff != -1` promotes to `65535 != -1` = always true.
The asm is a 16-bit `cmp word[2da2],0xffff; jne`. So EVERY `DAT_2000_2da2 == -1` / `!= -1` in the
decompile is wrong (10 sites: 15514/15572/15625/15699/15786/15912/16009/16075/31346/64457, plus
2da6 at 14001/64464).  FIX: compare against 0xffff, not -1 (undefined2 is unsigned).

Once 2da2 is correctly -1, a5dc runs its count-path -- which is ALSO base-lost (asm 0x1a61e-0x1a664):
  - the side-count walk read the registry object near offset as a HOST pointer at int*-stride 8
    (asm: si=word[DGROUP:bx]; test byte[DGROUP:si+0x17],8; STRIDE 4);
  - the HUD write `es:[0x2d8e]=ax` dropped ES=word[DGROUP:0x70] (the str-seg) -> wild host write to 0x2d8e.
REBUILT both (DGROUP + str-seg).  RESULT: the side-count works (max5790=16) and a5dc's win-check is live.

BUT: applying the signedness fix ALSO opens the other 2da2==-1 gates (15514 etc.), which guard flight-model
logic that has its OWN latent base-losses -- and running it changes the (chaotic) combat trajectory so the
AI-vs-AI engagement STALLS at ~2 kills (min_a296=14) instead of eliminating the side.  So the signedness
fix is CORRECT but exposes a base-loss cascade in the 2da2-gated flight-model functions (same pattern as
the c31e hit-cluster).  NEXT: fix those gated functions' base-losses so the combat resolves faithfully with
the win-logic active -> then a814 fires (578e->0) -> mission self-terminates.

The a5dc rebuild (count walk + str-seg write) is saved below for re-application with the cascade fix.
